{"data": [{"author_id": "2114906570303905792", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:22:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118499245275914596"], "id": "2118499245275914596", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1751810001751183361", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118390707228745948", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cognition A cheaper review loop lowers the friction for smaller teams, but adoption still depends on catching the hard edge cases.", "url": "https://x.com/BudgtStore/status/2118499245275914596"}, {"author_id": "2019929179131699200", "created_at": "2026-11-05T23:15:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118482386929533318"], "id": "2118482386929533318", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1751810001751183361", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118390707228745948", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cognition Making PR review cheaper and faster hits the real bottleneck.", "url": "https://x.com/peteryantweets/status/2118482386929533318"}, {"author_id": "46498861", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:33:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118456692795162778"], "id": "2118456692795162778", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1751810001751183361", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118390707228745948", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cognition Cheaper and faster changes what review is for. At 5x cheaper, a review stops being a bottleneck you ration and becomes the default on every pull request. The human job then shifts from reading every line to judging whether the review caught what matters.", "url": "https://x.com/raulnogales/status/2118456692795162778"}, {"author_id": "221164134", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:30:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118456007517159735"], "id": "2118456007517159735", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1751810001751183361", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 70, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118390707228745948", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cognition Beautifully done, but I'm not sure line-by-line code review has much of a future", "url": "https://x.com/t1llmann/status/2118456007517159735"}, {"author_id": "2813056513", "created_at": "2026-11-05T19:34:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118426763676074317"], "id": "2118426763676074317", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1751810001751183361", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118390707228745948", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cognition Congrats on Review 2.0. I think creators engineers follow could introduce Devin's PR workflow. Chals Channel offers free creator search, campaign planning, briefs and proposals. Happy to map your first campaign to your goals and target customers", "url": "https://x.com/Ignaciosolere/status/2118426763676074317"}, {"author_id": "1825556649723240448", "created_at": "2026-11-05T19:19:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118422883840262275"], "id": "2118422883840262275", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1751810001751183361", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 58, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118390707228745948", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cognition 5x cheaper and 1.5x faster is a big jump — curious how much of a PR review it handles on its own now.", "url": "https://x.com/JMkernt/status/2118422883840262275"}, {"author_id": "2114261495278391296", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:21:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118408401256579287"],